      "noteEn": "The chart places the conventional Edad Moderna, modernism, mid-century modern, postmodernity, and a present-day “modern” segment along one chronology. Each label arose in a different historical or stylistic context, but their overlapping claims to modernity make the terminology look self-contradictory. The caption jokingly credits historians with this accumulation.",
